            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0776" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5747/35.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Panama to the Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Panama</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I am instructed by my Government to
                    propose to your excellency’s Government Mr. Edwin Denby as umpire of the mixed
                    commission mentioned in Articles VI and XV of the convention of November 18,
                    1903, which I do with great pleasure and the hope that Mr. Denby will be
                    acceptable to your excellency’s Government.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. Arango.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
